<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Komm, Gott Schöpfer, Heiliger Geist (Martin Luther)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1524</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (German paraphrase, melody derived from the chant)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English version attributed to Thomas Cranmer</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1550</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (Prayer Book Ordinal)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English version by John Cosin</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1625</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (sung at every British coronation since Charles I)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English version by John Dryden</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1693</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (Examen Poeticum)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Komm, Schöpfer Geist, kehr bei uns ein (Heinrich Bone)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1845</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (German paraphrase, adapted plainchant melody)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Komm, Heiliger Geist, der Leben schafft (Friedrich Dörr)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1972</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (German, melody close to the chant)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Veni creator (Jehan Titelouze)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1623</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (organ setting)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Veni creator Spiritus, five settings (Marc-Antoine Charpentier)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1670s-1690s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chorale prelude on Luther's chorale (Johann Pachelbel)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1693</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chorale BWV 370 and chorale preludes BWV 631 and 667 (Johann Sebastian Bach)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1708-1750</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (Luther's chorale)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Veni creator, motet H 141 (Hector Berlioz)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">c. 1861-1868</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Motet WAB 50 (Anton Bruckner)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">c. 1884</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (harmonized)</span></li></ul></section>
